                    },
                    "message": "set the first argument to the function as ipmi::Context::ptr &ctx so you can use the yielding dbus APIs."
                },
                {
                    "file": "apphandler.cpp",
                    "line": 756,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "Since the function is returning a bunch of bits, use the bit-packing API so you don't have to worry about masking and shifting and hard-coded offsets.\n```suggestion\n\nauto ipmiAppGetSelfTestResults(ipmi::Context::ptr& ctx) -> ipmi::RspType<\n  uint8_t, // self-test return value\n  uint1_t, // Controller operational firmware corrupted\n  uint1_t, // (bit 2)\n  uint1_t, // (bit 3)\n  uint1_t, // ... other value descriptions here...\n  uint1_t, // ...\n  uint1_t, // ...\n  uint1_t, // (bit 6)\n  uint1_t  // cannot access SEL device\n>\n```"
                },
